  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Tuesday) \nIssued at 943 AM CDT Tue Jul 28 2026\n\nThe real relief comes on Thursday and Friday as temperatures will\nbe in the mid to upper 80s with dewpoints falling into the low to\nmid 60s across the area. Conditions look to remain dry on both\ndays. Unfortunately, beginning on Friday night, rain and storm\nchances will return to Middle Tennessee as a very strong, at least\nfor this time of year, low pressure system works its way out of\nthe Midwest and right over our area. This system will bring with\nit a risk for excessive rainfall across the area. The WPC has\nalready outlined Middle Tennessee with a slight risk for excessive\nrainfall on Saturday. As for the risk for severe storms, there is\nnot a strong signal at this time, though it is worth watching for\nin future updates. Rain and thunderstorms chances are likely to\nstick around for the remainder of the forecast period.",
